WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
Are you okay with that?

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.680
I'm here to debate you, not debate them.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.620
I mean, you're all on the same side.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.460
You're part of one group.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.300
No.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.120
You've been clapping each other.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:06.960
No, I mean, there are conservatives here.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.180
There are far right people here.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.020
There are Republicans here.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:09.860
But how do you feel about that guy

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.680
wanting me and you to leave?

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.140
But, you know, let's stick-

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:12.980
I'm just wondering.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:13.800
This is the topic of immigration.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.640
It's not about my- How do you feel about the guy?

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.660
It's not about my feelings towards them.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.500
Okay.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.320
It's about staying on this topic.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.160
Okay.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.360
And talk about- Immigrants are good for America, yeah.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.040
You and me, we're good for America.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.080
And the guy over there wants us to leave.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.280
So I'm just wondering how you feel about that.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.120
So I believe that there has to be

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.520
strict immigration laws.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.360
Okay.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.119
We have to make sure that the people are coming here

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:34.799
have the good intent of the United States in mind.

00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:35.959
That's not my claim, but okay.

00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:36.799
So-

00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:38.000
My claim is about immigrants are net positive.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.439
If you just open our borders to every single person

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:41.480
that wants to be here- No one calls for open borders.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.860
You know, that claims that they have

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.279
economical hardship in their country.

00:00:44.279 --> 00:00:46.080
Who's calling for open borders?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:46.919
I'm just saying, you know-

00:00:46.919 --> 00:00:48.119
Oh, I mean, it's a straw man.

00:00:48.119 --> 00:00:49.439
So you're just saying a straw man.

00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:50.279
No, I'm saying that if-

00:00:50.279 --> 00:00:51.599
You're wasting time with a straw man.

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:52.599
No one's calling for open borders.

00:00:52.599 --> 00:00:53.439
I didn't call for open borders.

00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:54.259
Well, you wasted time-

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.860
You wasted time trying to cause division

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.060
between me and my friend over here.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:58.900
Division?

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.720
He wants you to leave the country.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.020
That's a pretty big deal.

